From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Mon, 26 Oct 2026 02:41:40 +0000
Subject: Update ICU to 2a51536df

Brings ICU up to upstream chromium/deps/icu 2a51536df, which includes:

* 8cc91d9b6 [ICU] Exclude unused nfkc_scf.nrm from ICU data bundle
* 6ebb40c59 Update tzdata to 2026c and rebuild data files.
* 794156e5a Add kojii to `OWNERS`
* 5aa526207 Update TZDB to 2024d (tzdata 2026d despite the subject)
* 19dfb44a6 Update tzdata to 2026e
* 83ffaeb85 [icu] Fix signed int32_t overflow in CharString
* 4fe960221 [icu] Fix Chromium License Check
* 2a51536df [Windows] Update windowsZone.txt

tzdata 2026e maps Europe/London and Europe/Dublin to the GMT metazone.
Without it they map only to the British and Irish metazones, which have
no English winter name, so after daylight saving time ends ICU formats
their long time zone name as "GMT+00:00" instead of "Greenwich Mean
Time". The CharString change hardens capacity calculations against
signed 32-bit overflow, and the windowsZones update fixes automatic time
zone detection on Windows.

The tree matches upstream 2a51536df except for prebuilt data that
Electron's build does not use, which is left unchanged: the icudtl.dat
files for other platforms (android, cast, chromecast_video, chromeos and
ios), the big-endian common/icudtb.dat, and the standalone time zone
resources in tzres/. patches/charstr.patch, upstream's record of the
CharString change, is also left out because its blank context lines trip
Electron's trailing whitespace check; the change itself is in
source/common/charstr.cpp. common/icudtl.dat is upstream's.

This patch can be removed once Chromium's DEPS ICU revision is
2a51536df or later.

